WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.500
Thailand sits at the center of mainland Southeast Asia, celebrated for its sacred Buddhist temples.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Doi Inthanon in Chiang Mai rises to 2,565 meters in the misty Thanon Thong Chai range.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.000
Historic Ayutthaya and Sukhothai preserve UNESCO-listed ruins of royal palaces and chedis.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:23.000
Traditional Chut Thai attire is woven from Khorat Thai silk with gold brocade sabai shawls.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Iconic gastronomy includes savory Pad Thai noodles and zesty Tom Yum Goong lemongrass soup.

